  "id": "empathic-failure",
  "term": "empathic failure",
  "definition": "Empathic failure is a breakdown in a clinician’s felt ability to attune to or connect with a patient during the clinical encounter. In this source, it is described as a key experiential aspect of praecox feeling and as a subjective disruption in empathic attunement that may contribute to recognizing schizophrenia.",
